From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Accept input again once a video decoder drain
 completed.

The unix transform refuses input while draining (STATUS_DEVICE_BUSY,
MF_E_NOTACCEPTING) and leaves that state only on a flush. An MFT takes
input again once its drain is complete, and the source reader can drain
an empty decoder that nobody flushes afterwards: at the end of a stream
it drains the decoder; the application seeks back to the start, the
reader flushes; the application's next ReadSample requests a sample
before the media source has restarted, gets MF_E_END_OF_STREAM and
drains the decoder again; the seek's MEStreamSeeked then only notifies
the start of stream. Every input of the new pass is refused, the
playback stops on the last frame.

When ProcessOutput gets STATUS_END_OF_FILE (the drain is complete),
flush the transform so that it takes input again.

Game impacted: Big Foot Crush (UNIS, Unity 2022): its attract movie
(looped by Unity's VideoPlayer with a seek to 0 at the end) stopped on
its last frame after one to a few loops (GE-Proton11-10 and 11-12);
eight loops in a row with the patch.
---
--- a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
@@ -1671,6 +1671,9 @@
     }
     else if (ntstatus == STATUS_END_OF_FILE)
     {
+        /* The drain is complete: the decoder takes input again, as after a flush (the source
+         * reader may drain an empty decoder again, from a sample request racing a seek). */
+        winedmo_transform_flush(decoder->winedmo_transform);
         samples->dwStatus = MFT_OUTPUT_DATA_BUFFER_NO_SAMPLE;
         hr = MF_E_TRANSFORM_NEED_MORE_INPUT;
     }
